From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 10:03:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] fix: as_tibble() method for GInteractions

tibble::as_tibble(<GInteractions>) reached InteractionSet's S4
as.data.frame() method only because S4Vectors' S3 method
as.data.frame.Vector() dispatched again to the S4 generic. S4Vectors 0.51.10
(Bioconductor 3.24) no longer does, and InteractionSet has no S3 method of
its own, so as_tibble(gi) fails with 'no method for coercing this S4 class to
a vector'. That broke write_bedpe(), write_pairs(), the 'Reverting from
GInteractions to tabular data frames' section of the vignette, and users'
code.

as_tibble.GInteractions() goes through BiocGenerics::as.data.frame()
explicitly. Results are unchanged on current Bioconductor.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FLbRhpc2hEajWKBL7zXM8Q
